[
  {
    "type": "heading",
    "defaultValue": "PulseTime Face"
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "defaultValue": "Start with the bright, large clock. Tap the watch twice in the same direction within about a second to feel the time. Keep this face on screen while listening. To change anything, open PulseTime Face settings in the Pebble phone app, choose your options, and tap Save to watch."
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Learn the first pattern"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "The starting pattern counts the hour with short pulses, pauses, then counts completed quarters with longer pulses. At 3:30, feel three short pulses, a pause, then two long pulses. At 3:00 there are no quarter pulses. It reports the completed quarter, so 3:44 feels like 3:30 until you enable exact minutes. Haptic hours always use 1–12, even when the visible clock uses 24-hour time."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "Practice while looking at the clock. Count the hour first, then the quarter. Try Slow if pulses run together. For guided examples, pattern comparisons, and button shortcuts, open the separate PulseTime watchapp."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "defaultValue": "The face uses double-taps. Pebble keeps its normal side-button actions: it does not let a watchface remap those buttons. Choose PulseTime in the watch’s Quick Launch settings for a shortcut to the interactive watchapp."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Make the clock easy to see"
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "STYLE",
        "label": "Clock layout",
        "defaultValue": "bold",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Bold — hours above minutes",
            "value": "bold"
          },
          {
            "label": "Classic — time in one row",
            "value": "classic"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Bold uses large, thick digits on rectangle and round screens. Hours are the top pair; minutes are the bottom pair. The watch’s own 12/24-hour preference is used."
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "THEME",
        "label": "Contrast",
        "defaultValue": "bright",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Bright — black on white",
            "value": "bright"
          },
          {
            "label": "Dark — white on black",
            "value": "dark"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Both choices use full contrast, including on the monochrome Pebble 2 SE. Bright is the default. This changes the colors, not the watch’s backlight setting."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Choose a pattern"
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "SYSTEM",
        "label": "Time system",
        "defaultValue": "terse_quarter",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Terse Quarter (hours, quarters)",
            "value": "terse_quarter"
          },
          {
            "label": "Five-Minute Ladder",
            "value": "five_minute_ladder"
          },
          {
            "label": "Decimal Place Rhythm",
            "value": "decimal_place"
          },
          {
            "label": "Binary Clock",
            "value": "binary_clock"
          },
          {
            "label": "Nearest-Quarter Offset",
            "value": "nearest_quarter"
          },
          {
            "label": "Morse Digits",
            "value": "morse_digits"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Start with Terse Quarter for fewer pulses. Five-Minute Ladder is exact but can be long. Decimal Place reads minute digits with a long pulse for zero. Binary and Morse suit people who already know those codes. Nearest-Quarter uses an offset and takes more practice. A motor has one strength; distinguish patterns by timing and pauses."
      },
      {
        "type": "select",
        "messageKey": "SPEED",
        "label": "Playback speed",
        "defaultValue": "standard",
        "options": [
          {
            "label": "Slow",
            "value": "slow"
          },
          {
            "label": "Standard",
            "value": "standard"
          },
          {
            "label": "Fast",
            "value": "fast"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Slow stretches every pulse and pause by 25%; Fast shortens them by 22%."
      },
      {
        "type": "toggle",
        "messageKey": "EXACT_MINUTES",
        "label": "Exact minutes (Terse Quarter only)",
        "defaultValue": false,
        "description": "Adds short ticks after the quarter for leftover minutes: 3:32 adds two ticks after the two quarter pulses. This takes longer, especially near the next quarter. The other systems already report exact minutes."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "section",
    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "defaultValue": "Double-tap to feel the time"
      },
      {
        "type": "toggle",
        "messageKey": "TAP_TELL",
        "label": "Double-tap to tell time",
        "defaultValue": true,
        "description": "Tap twice in the same direction within about a second. Single taps and taps during playback are ignored. Turn this off if ordinary movement triggers it, or to reduce accelerometer use."
      }
    ]
  },
